Debian MTA SHOULD-commands — future enhancement
================================================

dsmr-qmail-run claims the mail-transport-agent role and ships:

  * /usr/sbin/sendmail  -> /usr/sbin/qmail-sendmail   (required; faithful)
  * /usr/bin/mailq      -> /usr/sbin/qmail-qstat      (best-effort)
  * /usr/sbin/newaliases -> fastforward qmail-newaliases (rebuilds aliases.cdb)

mailq remains an approximation and should be improved:

  - mailq: qmail-qstat reports queue counts, not the per-message mailq(8)
    listing.  A wrapper that renders qmail-qread output in mailq format would
    be a faithful replacement.

newaliases now delegates to fastforward's qmail-newaliases (Recommended by this
package) when present, rebuilding /etc/aliases.cdb from /etc/aliases; it is a
no-op only when fastforward is absent or there is no /etc/aliases.

Until then the stubs satisfy "default-mta | mail-transport-agent" dependents
without breaking programs that call these commands.

Man pages
---------
sendmail(8), mailq(1), and newaliases(8) currently have no man pages in this
package (lintian no-manual-page is overridden).  Ship man pages alongside the
faithful command implementations above.
